flavour|coalition_flight_doctrine	0	Every League member world sends its own carrier detachment to a joint fleet, and the League's flight doctrine makes them fly as one: a bomber from one world takes orders from a flight lead from another. Pilots from rival worlds fly together mostly so each can report on the other.
flavourAutomated|coalition_flight_doctrine	0	Every League member world sends its own carrier detachment to a joint fleet, and the League's flight doctrine makes them fly as one. The ship's core records the doctrine from joint fleet comm traffic and flies its own wings by it. It has no rival world to report back to.
type|coalition_flight_doctrine|null|0	0	When this ship deploys, its wings that share a role lend each other strikecraft. Each wing keeps at least 1 of its own strikecraft and fills the rest of its normal wing size with up to <good>1</good> of every other strikecraft type in its group. All its wings use the engagement range of its longest-ranged wing. Strikecraft in each group fly at the group's average top speed.
