flavour|concussion_shells	0	Planetary defense batteries on Eventide fire heavy shells with a delayed charge that bursts just inside the plating, shaking loose whatever is mounted nearby. A retired battery sergeant teaches the crew to pack them in exchange for passage off-world. The sergeant asks not to be told where the shells end up.
flavourAutomated|concussion_shells	0	Planetary defense batteries on Eventide fire heavy shells with a delayed charge that bursts just inside the plating, shaking loose whatever is mounted nearby. The ship's core copies the fusing tables from a salvaged battery fire-control unit, and the refit crew packs the shells to match. The unit is still listed as in service.
type|concussion_shells|null|0	0	Large ballistic weapon hits on an enemy ship's armor or hull have a <good>10%</good> chance to disable the weapon or engine nearest the impact.
