flavour|hold_the_line	0	Hegemony line drill holds that a battle line which keeps station cannot be broken, only worn down. The crew posts damage-control teams behind the forward armor and learns to stop the ship when the shooting starts. Navy instructors call this courage. Navy accountants call it cheaper than engines.
flavourAutomated|hold_the_line	0	Hegemony line drill holds that a battle line which keeps station cannot be broken, only worn down. The ship's core studies recordings of Navy lines under fire, and the refit crew braces the forward armor for a ship that stops when the shooting starts. Navy instructors call this courage. Navy accountants call it cheaper than engines.
type|hold_the_line|null|0	0	<good>15%</good> reduced armor damage taken while moving slower than 25% of top speed.
