flavour|navy_heartbeat	0	Sailing alongside Hegemony battle lines teaches the crew the Navy's habit of arriving at speed and firing before the enemy has settled, guns thumping out what the Navy calls its heartbeat.
flavourAutomated|navy_heartbeat	0	The ship's core logs hours of Hegemony line engagements and reproduces the Navy's habit of arriving at speed and firing before the enemy has settled, guns thumping out what the Navy calls its heartbeat. The core keeps time more evenly than any Navy gunner.
