flavour|nskr_absorption	0	Disassembling the ABSORB loop from a Kingstork taught the crew how to bank the energy their shields block instead of venting it, and how to spend it on the guns.
flavourAutomated|nskr_absorption	0	Disassembling the ABSORB loop from a Kingstork showed the refit crew how to bank the energy the shields block instead of venting it. The ship's core decides when to spend it on the guns.
type|nskr_absorption|null|0	0	Flux taken by the shield charges a reserve of up to 1000, which drains by 100 per second. While charged, up to <good>50%</good> increased ballistic and energy weapon rate of fire, at full strength from 500 reserve. Non-beam weapons also cost less flux per shot, so their faster fire costs no extra flux.
