flavour|tania_carina_charge	0	War, war never changes. In order to survive the Luddic Path mayhem, Carina Forces had to act fast, or expire. Your crew learns from these hit and run tactics, and by executing them at high speeds, they exploit enemy weaknesses.
type|tania_carina_charge|null|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
type|tania_carina_charge|FRIGATE|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
type|tania_carina_charge|DESTROYER|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
type|tania_carina_charge|CRUISER|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
type|tania_carina_charge|CAPITAL_SHIP|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
flavour|tania_dysis_drive	0	The Black Hawk's Dysis Drive throws the ship forward hardest while its flux grid runs cold. Analysis over its ancient design allowed the crew to tune this ship's engines the same way, so it is able to fly bright at low flux and drags once the grid fills.
type|tania_dysis_drive|FRIGATE|0	0	Top speed changes with flux, from <good>+50</good> su/s at no flux to <bad>-50</bad> su/s at full flux, with no change at half flux. Below half flux, also up to <good>50%</good> increased acceleration and turn acceleration.
type|tania_dysis_drive|DESTROYER|0	0	Top speed changes with flux, from <good>+40</good> su/s at no flux to <bad>-40</bad> su/s at full flux, with no change at half flux. Below half flux, also up to <good>40%</good> increased acceleration and turn acceleration.
type|tania_dysis_drive|CRUISER|0	0	Top speed changes with flux, from <good>+30</good> su/s at no flux to <bad>-30</bad> su/s at full flux, with no change at half flux. Below half flux, also up to <good>30%</good> increased acceleration and turn acceleration.
type|tania_dysis_drive|CAPITAL_SHIP|0	0	Top speed changes with flux, from <good>+20</good> su/s at no flux to <bad>-20</bad> su/s at full flux, with no change at half flux. Below half flux, also up to <good>20%</good> increased acceleration and turn acceleration.
flavour|tania_fafnir_breeches	0	Desperation leads to innovation, and the pressure of an incoming war brought Farige engineers to the limit, with them bringing up unusual techniques to modernize recently found early epoch Domain designs. Mount plans traded by Navarchy quartermasters had a complete data basis of prototype adaptive weapon mounts, allowing ballistic weapon systems to draw harder from the ship's flux grid in order to field energy based weaponry.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|null|0	0	Ballistic weapon mounts become hybrid mounts.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|null|1	1	<good>25%</good> increased ballistic weapon flux cost.
