flavour|xiv_torpedo_doctrine	0	XIV Battlegroup strike manuals, kept by the Hegemony since the Domain, teach that a torpedo should close fast and fly straight. Following them, the crew rewires each missile's maneuvering thrusters to push it forward instead, on the principle that a missile which cannot turn must not miss.
flavourAutomated|xiv_torpedo_doctrine	0	XIV Battlegroup strike manuals, kept by the Hegemony since the Domain, hold that a torpedo should close fast and fly straight. The refit crew rewires each missile's maneuvering thrusters to push it forward instead, on the principle that a missile which cannot turn must not miss.
